timesheet source package
========================

Two upstream tarballs, both built by debian/make-orig-tarballs.sh:

 * timesheet_<ver>.orig.tar.xz: the repository, without debian/.
 * timesheet_<ver>.orig-vendor.tar.xz: every crate in Cargo.lock, unpacked to
   vendor/. Launchpad's builders have no network. Crates that only build for
   Windows, macOS or WebAssembly are reduced to their Cargo.toml and an
   empty lib.rs.

The script also regenerates the vendor/ paragraphs of debian/copyright, and
prints the upstream version, <Cargo.toml version>+git<date>.<sha>.

One debian/ serves noble, resolute and stonking. debian/changelog is kept at
the plain version with distribution UNRELEASED; each upload sets the top
entry to <ver>-1~ppa1~ubuntu<YY.MM>.1 and the series name, for example:

  dch -b -v <ver>-1~ppa1~ubuntu24.04.1 -D noble "Build for noble."

Two CI pipelines publish from this source, one per forge. A push to GitHub
runs .github/ppa-upload, which uploads source packages for Launchpad to
build. A push to Forgejo runs .forgejo/registry-upload, which builds the
binary package itself in a container of each series and uploads the debs to
the Debian registry at forgejo.bobbalisa.org; both use the same version
scheme, so the same snapshot carries the same version in both archives.

